{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["כִּי הוּא מֹשֵׁל — and do not fear to come to him." "וְלֵב יַעֲקֹב פָּג — his heart changed, as if to say: this is not true, for he did not believe them — as in: אַל־תִּתְּנִי פוּגַת לָךְ. And וריחו לא נמר is translated: וריחו לא פג."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {1 "Rashbam's lemma is Gen 45:26 וַיָּגָל לִבּוֹ, vocalized by him as ויפג לבו, reading פוג in the sense of 'change/grow faint'; his prooftext is a form of פוג meaning 'cease/lag'; the Aramaic line refers to Targum Onkelos on Gen 27:12."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:23.494038674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}